================================================================
V9 CAMPAIGN LOG — mid-game (turn-3+) adjacency/outs take rule
Opened 2026-09-04. Prior campaign: results/v8_gates.log (v8home).
================================================================

--- REGISTRATION (2026-09-04, BEFORE any study launch) ---

User idea: hand adjacency as a strength proxy; take-vs-draw should
weigh the upcard's adjacency against how many good draws (outs)
remain unseen. Generalize the turn-2 book to mid-game free-draw
nodes (j >= 2), conditioning on outs.

Definitions (all hero-observable):
  free-draw node: hero to move, non-opening, legal kinds ==
    {DrawCardAction, PickUpDiscardAction}; j = 1-based index of the
    hand's free-draw nodes (j=1 is the t2-book node).
  adj(hand, top) = # hand cards rank-mates of top OR same suit
    within 2 ranks (the book metric).
  outs(hand, seen) = # unseen cards c with min_deadwood(hand+[c])
    <= min_deadwood(hand); seen = hand | pile | opp.known_cards
    (FULL observable; outs_pileonly recorded as nat2 bridge).
  melds = min_deadwood(hand+[top]) <= min_deadwood(hand).
  topv = DEADWOOD_VALUE[top]. d = T - D (forced take minus forced
    draw, both arms played to hand end by v8home both seats).

Instrument: turn3_study.py — census-then-fork. Census plays the
deal to the END on the champion line recording every free-draw
node + the bot's natural choice; ONE node k is picked uniformly
among eligible nodes (j>=2; cell-matching in --cell mode) by
random.Random(deal_seed*2+1); both arms replay to node k (identity
asserted vs census), forced, finished. One row per deal.

Pre-registered hypotheses:
  C1 (PRIMARY, suppression): in cell (bot_takes & ~melds),
     dEV(take) < 0. Margins: pooled + one-dim splits outs {0-4,
     5-8, 9+}, adj {<=1, >=2}, topv {<=3, 4-7, 8-10}, turn
     {j=2, 3-4, 5+}. Interactions exploratory.
  C2 (generalized t2 clause): in (~melds & topv<=3 & adj>=2),
     dEV(take) > 0.
  C2b (SECONDARY, the user's outs variant): same cell & outs<=4,
     dEV(take) > 0. Chosen over C2 only if it clearly dominates on
     CONFIRMATION rows. [K=4 was to be primary; the phase-0 nat2
     reslice (nat2_reslice.py, 430 rows) shows the turn-2 cell is
     positive across ALL outs bins (outs>2: +3.14 +/- 2.50; OLS
     slope -0.08 +/- 1.19) and the outs<=2 +10.96 slice is n=24 —
     not a robust trend, so the un-gated clause is registered as
     primary exception and outs-gating must earn its place at
     turn 3+.]
  C3 (dose-response, the user's mechanism direct test): within
     (~melds & adj>=2), OLS slope of d on outs is negative.

Operational rule (the only thing that can reach a gate):
  t3_book_take(hand, top, seen) = melds OR (topv<=3 AND adj>=2
  [AND outs<=4 iff C2b dominates C2 on confirmation rows]),
  applied as a full override at free-draw nodes j>=2 (it both
  vetoes all other non-melding search takes — the C1 direction —
  and forces the exception takes).

Decision rule: advance to confirmation iff C1-pooled or C2 has a
95% CI excluding 0 with the predicted sign on the selection rows.
Anything else found in the rows is exploratory and re-enters at
confirmation with its own fresh seed. If nothing fires: close the
campaign with a power statement.

Seeds (all residue-distinct mod 977 from every base used in v8):
  90000 uniform selection study   92000 targeted C2 study
  94000 confirmation              96000 t3_gate selection
  98000 t3_gate confirmation
  ps multiplier: seed*10141 + tries*19 (fresh vs 7211/9013).

Gate protocol: t3_gate.py (t2_gate clone), hero
HomeV8Policy(t3book=True) vs False, champion opponent, paired
deals. >=-tie adoption allowed only because the causal evidence is
same-distribution (methodology rule 4) AND the fire-rate x
per-fire dilution estimate from the census is consistent with the
gate number. Positive gates confirm fresh at 98000. If the rule
fires too rarely for a gate to resolve, adoption on causal
evidence alone per the t2 low-card precedent.

