=== CAMPAIGN CLOSED 2026-09-04 — VERDICT ===

1. The user's adjacency/outs conditioning hypothesis: NEGATIVE at
   every registered test. Outs level does not detectably modulate
   take value at turn 2 (flat reslice) or mid-game (flat C3, C2b
   wrong sign). Adjacency itself already carries the value the
   books capture (t2 low-card clause stands untouched).
2. The t2 low-card exception does NOT generalize to j>=2
   (C2 -2.70 +/- 8.28, wrong sign).
3. NEW POSITIVE KNOWLEDGE: the mid-game TAKE/DRAW side of open
   frontier #2 is now AUDITED AND CLEAN. 3000 forced-arm paired
   deals (2000 uniform j>=2 + 1000 cell-targeted j=2) show the
   search's own draw-node choices are within noise of optimal on
   its own line: bot-takes-no-meld pooled -1.36 +/- 3.97 (uniform)
   and -0.80 +/- 2.36 (j=2 targeted); counterfactual no-meld takes
   the bot already declines cost -4.08 +/- 1.65 (it is right to
   decline them); melding takes +12.41 +/- 3.82 (it takes 100%).
   The early-game bias series (j=1 ~-1.9/take) decays below
   measurement by j=2, as the v8 log predicted. NO BOOK CHANGE.
   v8home remains the champion, unchanged.
4. Remaining frontier #2 item: mid-game discard SAFETY (feeding
   the opponent) — never forced-arm audited; separate instrument.
5. Kept: turn3_study.py (census-then-fork — the reusable mid-game
   forced-arm instrument, 0 replay mismatches over 3000 forks),
   turn3_confirm.py, nat2_reslice.py, and the row files (full
   observable state stored: any future mid-game take rule can be
   re-sliced OFFLINE from results/turn3_rows.jsonl +
   turn3_confirm_rows.jsonl before spending compute).
   Seeds 92000/96000/98000 retired unused.

