--- REGISTRATION: K-study (knock timing), seed 100000 ---

Mechanistic prior: the knock/continue choice is made by the search
whose T=16 deadwood leaf caused the confirmed turn-1/2 over-taking
(it overweights banked deadwood vs the gin race); full-rules
undercut swings +/-25-50/hand; the home game is gin-dominated.

Instrument knock_study.py (census-then-fork):
  Node: hero to move, legal contains >=1 KnockAction and >=1
  non-knock action, NO GinAction (gin is mandatory). Sample ONE
  such node per hand uniformly (random.Random(deal_seed*2+1));
  j = 1-based knock-node index.
  Arm K: force the BEST KNOCK (min residual deadwood, judge order
  on ties — the expert._candidates/MixedKnock rule).
  Arm C: force FastTeacher.act(game, non-knock legal) (the
  search's own prior discard; caveat: EV(C) is a mild lower bound
  on continue-EV when v8 would discard differently — biases the
  study TOWARD knocking looking good, so a confirmed
  "bot over-knocks" finding is conservative).
  Both arms finish with v8home both seats; paired per deal; full
  observable state stored per row.
Hypotheses:
  KA (bot knocks): dEV(K-C) on the bot's own knocks — leak iff
     mean < 0 with 95% CI excluding 0 (over-knocking).
  KB (bot continues): dEV(K-C) on the bot's declines — leak iff
     mean > 0, CI excluding 0 (under-knocking).
  Margins (one-dim): threshold {A-3, 4-7, 8-10}, stock {>=20,
  10-19, <10}, best-knock residual dw {0-3, 4-6, 7-10}, j {1, 2+}.
Decision rule: any registered cell firing -> fresh-seed
confirmation at 104000 before any rule/gate work.

--- REGISTRATION: D-study (discard safety), seed 102000 ---

Instrument discard_study.py (census-then-fork):
  Node: hero discard node (11 cards, no knock legal, len(legal)>1).
  Sample one per hand uniformly.
  Challenger: among legal discards whose resulting min-deadwood
  <= best+1, the one minimizing _live_count(card, hero-unseen
  pool) (ties: higher deadwood value); REJECT the node if it
  equals the bot's natural discard.
  Arms: bot's natural discard vs challenger; d = EV(chall)-EV(bot).
Hypotheses:
  DA (pooled): safety-first discarding gains: mean d > 0, CI
     excluding 0.
  Margins: opp visible pickups {0, >=1}, stock bands, threshold
  bands, dw-cost of challenger {0, 1}.
Decision rule: as K-study; confirmation seed 106000.

Seed hygiene: 100000/102000/104000/106000 mod 977 =
346/392/438/484, distinct from all used bases.

--- K-STUDY RESULT (2026-09-05): KNOCK TIMING AUDITED CLEAN ---

knock_study.py, 2000 paired deals, seed 100000, 240 min, 0 dupes,
0 replay mismatches. Log: results/knock_study.log; rows:
results/knock_rows.jsonl. Knock-option nodes: 3.0/hand; bot knocks
at 20.8% of them.
  KA (bot knocks):   dEV(K-C) +5.60 +/- 2.45  -> its knocks are
     RIGHT (positive, CI excludes 0 the healthy way). No margin
     fires the leak direction (kdw 0-3: -1.20 +/- 6.82 n=69 and
     j2+: -3.58 +/- 9.33 n=36 straddle 0).
  KB (bot continues): dEV(K-C) -10.42 +/- 1.40 -> its declines are
     RIGHT everywhere (all margins -6.8 to -13.3, all negative).
VERDICT: no leak. Knock/continue is a measured STRENGTH — the
deadwood-leaf over-taking mechanism does NOT extend to knock
timing. Caveat noted at registration: arm C uses the teacher's
continue-discard, biasing the study TOWARD knocking looking good —
which makes the KB (patience) result conservative and the KA
result mildly flattered; KA's +5.60 exceeds the plausible bias.
D-study (discard safety, seed 102000) launches next.

--- D-STUDY RESULT (2026-09-05): DISCARD SAFETY AUDITED CLEAN ---

discard_study.py, 2000 paired deals, seed 102000, 0 dupes, 0
replay divergences (wall-clock inflated by a ~9h machine sleep;
compute ~3.5h). Log: results/discard_study.log; rows:
results/discard_rows.jsonl. Eligible nodes (safety-first
challenger differs from bot's discard): 3.0/hand.
  DA pooled: dEV(safety-first - bot) = -3.47 +/- 1.65 -> the
  challenger LOSES; CI excludes 0 on the healthy side. Every
  registered margin negative (opp-pickups>=1 -4.10 +/- 2.05;
  deadwood-TIED swaps -3.53 +/- 1.83; even live-saved>=3 -4.16).
VERDICT: no leak. The bot's discard choice among near-tied cards
carries real value the live-count safety heuristic destroys
(opponent-live cards are usually hero-live too — naive safety
sacrifices own draw structure). Consistent with lesson #12's
standalone tie for belief-aware safety discarding; now confirmed
at the ROOT decision with forced arms. Confirmation seed 106000
retired unused.

=== LEAK HUNT CLOSED 2026-09-05 — VERDICT ===

All decision surfaces of v8home are now forced-arm audited:
  opening (book, v8)  |  j=1 take (book, v8)  |  j>=2 take/draw
  (v9 ph1+3, clean)  |  knock timing (K-study, clean — a measured
  STRENGTH: knocks +5.60 +/- 2.45, declines avoid -10.42 +/- 1.40)
  |  discard safety (D-study, clean).
NO systematic misplay remains at measurable size on the bot's own
line. The turn-1/turn-2 over-taking was the exception, not the
pattern, and the books already fixed it. By elimination, the
~14 pt/hand oracle gap is INFORMATION, not decision rules:
mid-game hand-reading + endgame play under uncertainty. The
standing structural direction (HANDOFF_V8 frontier #1, Track A
subgame CFR / belief-conditioned endgame) is where the points are.
Instruments kept: knock_study.py, discard_study.py (+ turn3_*),
all row files re-sliceable offline. 10,000+ forced-arm forks this
campaign, 0 replay mismatches.

