POSTERIOR GROUND-TRUTH CHECK (2026-09-05, user direction): the
first exact Bayesian-consistency test of the PF belief — compare
P_PF(opp hand | info set) against the EMPIRICAL conditional from
rejection-sampled deals reaching the same info set on the v8home
deployment line. Registered before launch. Instrument:
posterior_check.py. Design rules: screens are implication-only
(no forcing, no teacher screens — both bias a posterior study);
hero side fixed by construction (= conditioning on hero's
knowledge); hero policy seed FIXED (900001), opp seed fresh per
sample; accept iff the trajectory reproduces the target
hero-observable history exactly, early-abort on divergence.
================================================================

FROZEN SCENARIOS (from natural v8 self-play, picker seed 107000,
hero=P1 in both; ids are sim card ids):
  S1 (decline evidence, deal 107000): hero hand
     [0,8,21,25,29,31,34,38,46,48], flip 15 (thresh 3). Events:
     my-pass, opp-pass. Acceptance = opp book-pass (pure function,
     no search). N target 200,000.
  S2 (take+discard evidence, deal 107002): hero hand
     [2,5,7,29,36,37,38,40,41,43], flip 30 (thresh 5), X=22.
     Events: my-pass, opp-pickup flip, opp-discard X. Screens:
     book-take(opp10), X in opp10. One searched opp move per
     survivor. N target 1500.
  S3 (mid-game decline+discard, deal 107000): D=26, C=25, Y=6.
     Events: my-pass, opp-pass, my-draw D, my-discard C, opp-draw,
     opp-discard Y. Screens: opp book-pass, stock-top==D, Y in
     opp10 or Y==next stock card. Hero's discard C asserted
     deterministic (fixed hero seed). Two searched opp moves per
     survivor. N target 1500.

REGISTERED METRICS (per scenario): M1 per-card reliability z vs
binomial SE, flag |z|>3 (41 comparisons), watch |z|>2; M2 Brier
(particle._brier_probe) of raw AND shrunk ensemble marginals vs
uniform baseline; M3 evidence-channel mass (rank-mates and
suit-within-2 of the declined/discarded cards; meld-mates of the
taken flip) predicted vs empirical with CIs — the actionable
over/under-reaction readout; M4 joint: opp-hand deadwood
distribution + knockable fraction, particle cloud vs truth.
PF side: read_regress.ensemble_marginal, filters=4 champion
DEFAULT_PF; sensitivity row filters=8 + shifted ensemble seed —
ensemble noise must be << flagged deviations.
Seeds: S1 108000, S2 110000, S3 112000 (mod 977 distinct from all
used). Any confirmed miscalibration becomes the NEXT campaign's
target (likelihood fix per v7 protocol), not this study's scope.

--- POSTERIOR CHECK RESULTS (2026-09-05) — THE BELIEF IS
SYSTEMATICALLY UNDER-CONFIDENT; every evidence channel too soft ---

S1 (200k exact samples, decline-only): PF captures 89% of node
info (Brier 0.1809 vs uniform 0.1844, achievable 0.1805). Flip-
adjacent mass PF 0.532 vs TRUE 0.421 (suit+-2), 0.383 vs 0.316
(rank-mates) — ~25% excess on cards the deterministic book pass
rules out (tau_p=0.1 softness leaves 10x weight on adj>=2 hands;
in self-play the book NEVER mismatches). M4 cloud deadwood dead-on
(57.5 vs 57.8). Ensemble noise 0.016 << deviations.
S2 (1500, take+discard): PF captures 69% of node info (0.1683 /
uni 0.1744 / ach 0.1656). Take evidence under-weighted: rank-mates
of taken 5D PF 0.724 vs TRUE 0.893. DISCARD-CHOICE COUNTERFACTUAL
missing: truth crushes dead high cards (KS 0.099, TC 0.119, KH
0.115, QS 0.161 — "would have discarded THAT instead of TH") while
PF leaves ~2x (0.16-0.25). Run-direction asymmetry: 7D PF 0.545 vs
true 0.449, 3D PF 0.328 vs true 0.454. M4 cloud 7.6 pts too MELDY
(51.8 vs 59.4).
S3 (1500, decline+discard mid-game): PF captures 60% of node info
(0.1731 / uni 0.1790 / ach 0.1692). ALL channels under-weighted:
declined-flip suit+-2 PF 0.781 vs TRUE 0.443; declined-KH
rank-mates 0.511 vs 0.292; discarded-7S rank-mates 0.646 vs 0.389
(7D: PF 0.235 vs TRUE 0.087). M4 cloud 4.8 pts too pessimistic
(50.8 vs 46.1). Hero-line note: hero's discard at fixed seed
reproduces only ~50% across hidden permutations (the search's
world-shuffle consumes actual pool list order) — conditioning on
hero-played-C is the deployment line, noted as a benign
entanglement.

=== VERDICT ===
Monotone: 89% -> 69% -> 60% of available information captured as
evidence accumulates — the PF UNDER-REACTS to every evidence type
(pass, take, discard), never over-reacts. Root-cause candidates,
in order: (1) tau_p=0.1 on opening events that are DETERMINISTIC
in deployment; (2) discard energy too soft (tau_d=2.0, mu=0.3) —
misses the discard-choice counterfactual that empirically crushes
dead high cards; (3) robustness clips (lik_floor=0.02, eps=0.05)
cap per-event evidence; (4) historical calibration targeted
STREAM Brier of the SHRUNK marginal — the raw cloud the search
samples was never the calibration objective. This is the first
concrete, measured entry point into the ~14 pt/hand oracle gap.
NEXT CAMPAIGN: likelihood sharpening, gated per the v7 protocol,
with these three frozen scenarios as permanent regression
benchmarks (posterior_check.py --report re-runs them offline from
the stored rows: results/post_s{1,2,3}_rows.jsonl).
